W44-149 Phase 1: Photo discriminator audit for 1418519 W44-117 admission
==========================================================================

DATE       2026-05-21
GIT_REV    2a303428fe46443d3d5dca26ec7925df579ed616  (W44-148 main)
HOST       lilith
TARGET_DIR $HOME/work/zen/jxl-encoder-shared-target
TSV        benchmarks/w44_149_photo_proxy_audit_2026-05-21.tsv
ANALYSIS   ~/.claude/projects/-home-lilith-work-zen-jxl-encoder/memory/w44_149_mechanism_a_proxy_audit_2026-05-21.md

PURPOSE
-------
Find a sub-discriminator that admits the 1418519 photo to the W44-117
EPF sharpness seed (closes -2.57 SSIM2 deficit per W44-147 audit) while
EXCLUDING 1025469 (W44-118 protected; -0.85 SSIM2 regression if W44-117
fires there) and the other 39 CID22 validation photos.

PROBE BATTERY (28 features per image)
-------------------------------------
Reused W44-91 + W44-96 ZenanalyzeProxies definitions (bit-equivalent to
zenanalyze tier1.rs):
- m3_colourfulness (Hasler-Süsstrunk sRGB u8)
- flat_color_block_ratio (per-channel range <= 4 on every 8x8)
- edge_density (Sobel BT.601 luma, threshold 30)

Plus mask1x1 percentiles (median, p10, p25, p75, p90) from the existing
pipeline's pixel_domain_loss path (computed once at d=5 e7 reference).

Plus auxiliary candidates (W44-149 additions, all O(W*H) cheap):
- mean_luma (BT.601)
- low_luma_ratio (Y < 32)
- high_luma_ratio (Y > 224)
- chroma_block_ratio (8x8 blocks with X+B variance > 0.001)
- XYB-plane variances (X/Y/B)
- xb_var_ratio ((var_x+var_b)/var_y)
- flat_x_block_ratio
- masking field percentiles
- high_freq_energy_ratio (Y plane)
- palette_log2_size

CORPUS
------
All 41 CID22-512 validation photos at
~/work/codec-corpus/CID22/CID22-512/validation/
(canonical reference set per W44-101 ledger).

CLASSES
-------
WANT    = 1418519.png — admit to W44-117 (closes -2.57 SSIM2 deficit)
REJECT  = 1025469.png — must stay excluded (W44-118 closed -0.85 SSIM2)
CONTROL = remaining 39 CID22 validation photos — default-suppress for
          safety (no measured W44-117 EV)

REPRO
-----
CARGO_TARGET_DIR=$HOME/work/zen/jxl-encoder-shared-target \
  cargo run --release \
    --features __pre_quantized \
    --example w44_149_photo_proxy_audit \
    --manifest-path jxl-encoder/Cargo.toml \
    > benchmarks/w44_149_photo_proxy_audit_2026-05-21.tsv

RUNTIME    ~6 minutes (41 EncoderPrecomputed::compute calls at d=5 e7)

KEY FINDING (full analysis in memory note)
------------------------------------------
SINGLE-AXIS CLEAN SPLITTER: `mask_p25 >= 85`

- 1418519 (WANT): mask_p25 = 88.880  ← FIRES
- 1025469 (REJECT): mask_p25 = 60.639 ← blocked
- nearest CONTROL: 7552578.png at 77.900 (gap = 10.98)
- all other 38 CONTROL photos at mask_p25 < 78

Fires on exactly 1 of 41 photos (1418519 only). Gap to next-closest
control is 11.0 percentage points — strong safety margin.

ALSO RAN: `mask_med >= 92.0`, `mask_p10 >= 71.0` (both fire on 1418519
only with similar safety margins). `mask_p25` chosen as primary
recommendation because the WANT-to-nearest-CONTROL gap is widest (10.98
vs mask_med's 0.85, mask_p10's 2.20).

ALSO RAN: Single-axis high_luma_ratio, mean_luma, fcbr, m3_colour —
NONE cleanly separate WANT from CONTROL (multiple CONTROL photos
land above WANT's value on every one).

VERDICT
-------
CLEAN DISCRIMINATOR EXISTS at proxy level: `mask_p25 >= 85`.

W44-150 Phase 2 (separate chunk) needs to:
1. Add a new admission path in vardct/encoder.rs:3867 (the W44-118
   is_screenshot gate site) that ALSO admits when:
     mask_p25(mask1x1) >= W44_150_PHOTO_W44_117_MASK_P25_MIN (85.0)
   AND target_distance >= 4.0 (avoid low-d where W44-120 already
   excludes screen content for the same reason).
2. Validate that admitting 1418519 actually moves SSIM2 (per W44-139,
   the +0.034 R divergence exists but ssim2-cost is unverified — Phase
   2 measurement must confirm before shipping).
3. Re-verify 1025469 e8/e9 d=4 stays byte-identical (W44-118
   protection set) since its mask_p25 = 60.64 fails the new gate.
4. Sweep the remaining 39 CONTROL CID22 photos at d=5/6 e7/e8/e9 to
   confirm zero unintended fires (predicted from this audit: zero).

CONCERN: Single-image discriminator (1 of 41). Could be brittle — the
PROXY threshold works for the AVAILABLE measurement set, but other
1418519-class photos (uniform-bright-smooth photos) in the wider corpus
universe might or might not benefit similarly. Phase 2 acceptance
should include a "broader corpus dry-run" on ~50 photos outside CID22
to confirm the gate firing rate stays low and predictable.

